Beginner workflow (for getting help from Codex)
------------------------------------------------

You can ask Codex to directly edit this project without manually pushing to GitHub first.

Recommended prompt template:
- Goal: what you want changed (bug fix, new feature, refactor)
- Scope: files/folders to touch (or say "find it for me")
- Done condition: how to verify (for example: `make` passes)

Example:
"Fix line-clear scoring in `Tetris_Game.cpp`, only change game logic, and make sure `make` succeeds."

GitHub remote setup is optional for local edits. It is only needed when you want to sync your local history with GitHub (`git push` / `git pull`).

Repository mismatch troubleshooting
---------------------------------

If you expected another project (for example `namidaru/cash-burner`) but Codex shows this Tetris codebase,
that means the current workspace folder is a different repository.

Quick checks:
- `pwd` (or Windows: `cd`) to see your current folder
- `git remote -v` to see which GitHub repository this folder is connected to

To work on `namidaru/cash-burner` in a fresh folder:
- `git clone https://github.com/namidaru/cash-burner.git`
- `cd cash-burner`

Then ask Codex to edit files in that repository path.

